  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 18 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, nothing is considered an offence if it is done by accident or misfortune, provided there is no criminal intention or knowledge involved in the act, which must be lawful and performed with proper care and caution. An illustration of this exception is provided where an individual using a hatchet accidentally causes harm without any lack of caution, making the act excusable and not an offence.",
